RapidSSL TLS RSA CA G1, the DigiCert intermediate that signs aplegislature.org's certificate.

Why it is here: from 17 Nov 2026 aplegislature.org serves its new certificate without this
intermediate, so a strict client cannot build the chain and the Legislature bills reader failed
("unable to get local issuer certificate", first on 22 Nov 2026). Browsers fetch the missing
intermediate themselves; Python does not. This file supplies exactly that one public
intermediate. The chain must still end at DigiCert Global Root G2 from certifi's store: see
_tls_context in base.py, which turns partial chains off, and tests/test_extra_intermediates.py.

Source: https://cacerts.digicert.com/RapidSSLTLSRSACAG1.crt.pem (the same file the site's
certificate names under "CA Issuers": http://cacerts.rapidssl.com/RapidSSLTLSRSACAG1.crt)
Subject: C=US, O=DigiCert Inc, OU=www.digicert.com, CN=RapidSSL TLS RSA CA G1
Issuer:  C=US, O=DigiCert Inc, OU=www.digicert.com, CN=DigiCert Global Root G2
Valid:   2 Nov 2017 to 2 Nov 2027
SHA-256: 44:22:E9:63:EE:53:CD:58:CC:9F:85:CD:40:BF:5F:FE:C0:09:5F:DF:1A:15:45:35:66:1C:1C:06:BC:AD:C6:9B
Checked 24 Nov 2026: with this file the handshake succeeds; without it, it fails.
